From b0749834efd3161472c21dbbf092c5da1f4ae58a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ut-bitra <ut-bitra@localhost>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:36:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] input: touchscreen: oplus: give WIDTH_MAJOR and
 PRESSURE a range

init_input_device() sets ABS_MT_WIDTH_MAJOR and ABS_MT_PRESSURE in
absbit, and touch reports send values for both. But only TOUCH_MAJOR,
POSITION_X and POSITION_Y got input_set_abs_params(), so the other two
axes reported min == max == 0.

Android's InputReader ignores this. libinput rejects the whole device:

  libinput error: event1 - touchpanel: kernel bug: device has min == max
  on ABS_MT_WIDTH_MAJOR

Under Ubuntu Touch, lomiri-system-compositor (Mir input-evdev, built on
libinput) therefore never opened the touchscreen, and the panel could
not be used even though the driver reported touches.

Both values come from the IC's u8 major field (struct point_info), so
use the same 0..255 range as TOUCH_MAJOR.

Verified on bitra: libinput now lists touchpanel (event1) with the
touch capability, lomiri-system-compositor holds event1, and touch
works in Lomiri.
---
 .../oplus_touchscreen/touchpanel_common_driver.c          | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/oplus_touchscreen/touchpanel_common_driver.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/oplus_touchscreen/touchpanel_common_driver.c
index f8cfda5e95ee..52b92b337c72 100755
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/oplus_touchscreen/touchpanel_common_driver.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/oplus_touchscreen/touchpanel_common_driver.c
@@ -6951,6 +6951,14 @@ static int init_input_device(struct touchpanel_data *ts)
 	}
 #endif
 	input_set_abs_params(ts->input_dev, ABS_MT_TOUCH_MAJOR, 0, 255, 0, 0);
+	/*
+	 * WIDTH_MAJOR and PRESSURE are declared in absbit above and reported
+	 * from the IC's u8 major value, but were never given a range, so the
+	 * kernel exposed min == max == 0. libinput rejects such a device as a
+	 * kernel bug, which leaves the touchscreen unusable outside Android.
+	 */
+	input_set_abs_params(ts->input_dev, ABS_MT_WIDTH_MAJOR, 0, 255, 0, 0);
+	input_set_abs_params(ts->input_dev, ABS_MT_PRESSURE, 0, 255, 0, 0);
 	input_set_abs_params(ts->input_dev, ABS_MT_POSITION_X, 0, ts->resolution_info.max_x - 1, 0, 0);
 	input_set_abs_params(ts->input_dev, ABS_MT_POSITION_Y, 0, ts->resolution_info.max_y - 1, 0, 0);
 	input_set_drvdata(ts->input_dev, ts);
